# Production Env
# Note: PB_URL is internal docker network or public URL.
# Since we are using client-side calls in Next.js, we usually need the public URL for the browser.
# But for verify/server-side, we might use internal.
# For simplicity, let's use the public URL that we plan to set up: https://hrv.demotesting.co.uk:8091 or via proxy.
# Wait, user instructions say ports 8091.
# And we are mapping 8091:8090.
# So public URL is http://hrv.demotesting.co.uk:8091 (until we secure it or proxy it).
# Let's assume standard public access for now.

NEXT_PUBLIC_PB_URL=https://pb.hrv.demotesting.co.uk
# Or if we proxy /api -> PB, it would be /api.
# The plan was 8091 exposed.
# BUT, we also mentioned proxying via Nginx.
# "Configure HestiaCP (Create domain, Proxy to Docker port)" -> Usually implies port 80/443 -> 3001 (Next.js).
# If Next.js talks to PB client-side, it needs a reachable PB URL.
# If we don't proxy PB, it's http://hrv.demotesting.co.uk:8091
# However, for HTTPS, we need SSL on 8091 or proxy it.
# Simplest Production setup:
# Next.js at https://hrv.demotesting.co.uk
# PocketBase at https://pb.hrv.demotesting.co.uk (requires 2nd domain) OR
# PocketBase at https://hrv.demotesting.co.uk/api/ (requires Nginx rewrites).
#
# Let's set it to the 8091 port for now, but valid HTTPS might be tricky without Hestia managing it.
# Actually, Hestia can manage multiple domains.
# Maybe we create `pb.hrv.demotesting.co.uk` later?
# For now I'll use the IP or domain:8091. BUT it wont have SSL easily.
#
# BETTER PLAN: Since implementation_plan said "Configure Nginx: Proxy to 3001", and "PocketBase: Port 8091".
# I'll stick to that.
PB_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
PB_ADMIN_EMAIL=mirza.ekm@gmail.com
